  42:src/can_comm.c **** /*
  43:src/can_comm.c ****  * Function:    CAN_Read_From_ECU
  44:src/can_comm.c ****  * Description: Reads vehicle status data from the ECU (Engine Control Unit) if a CAN message
  45:src/can_comm.c ****  *              has been received. Updates the global car_state structure.
  46:src/can_comm.c ****  * Returns:
  47:src/can_comm.c ****  *   - 1 if data was read and is within valid bounds.
  48:src/can_comm.c ****  *   - 0 if no new message or invalid data (out of range).
  49:src/can_comm.c ****  * Notes:
  50:src/can_comm.c ****  *   - The function uses CANisrFlag to determine if a new message was received.
  51:src/can_comm.c ****  *   - Performs range checks for RPM, gear, TPS, and VSS values.
  52:src/can_comm.c ****  *   - Clears the CANisrFlag after successful read.
